==Trivia==
*''Nobiru'' (伸びる) means "stretch", "extend" or "lengthen" in Japanese.
*Nobilan Pasalan's attack animation references three of the other [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Pasalans]]: his arms reference [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tesalan Pasalan]], his long neck references [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kubilan Pasalan]] and his legs reference [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Asilan Pasalan]].
**Nobilan Pasalan's arms and legs are longer than Tesalan Pasalan's and Asilan Pasalan's respectively, beating them at their own gimmicks aesthetically.
*Nobilan Pasalan is currently the tallest unit in the game, as seen during the second part of his multi-hit, where he stands up.
*Nobilan Pasalan has the second-longest piercing range of all cats, tied with [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]], as both of them are able to hit 500 range past their standing range. [[The 6th Angel (Uber Rare Cat)|The 6th Angel]] is in first place, with twice as much.
*Mystican Pasalan appears to be a reference to [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Hero_(Dragon_Quest_V) The Hero] from ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest V|Dragon Quest V]]'', as both wear similar turbans and capes and Mystican Pasalan's Japanese description suggests that he may be a wandering monster tamer.
**Mystican Pasalan's accessories are also reminiscent of [[wikia:hunterxhunter:Ging Freecss|Ging Freecss]] from ''[[wikipedia:Hunter × Hunter|Hunter × Hunter]]''.

